exports[`supi commands against a fake API, pinned > supi 020 boards (answered 403) (SUPERPIPELINE_AGENT_TOKEN) 1`] = `
{
  "exit": 1,
  "requests": [
    {
      "body": null,
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer spa_0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef",
        "Content-Type": "application/json",
      },
      "method": "GET",
      "url": "https://work.example/v1/boards",
    },
  ],
  "stderr": "Refused by superpipeline (403). {"error":{"code":"x","message":"refused for a reason"}}

This agent token does not permit that.
Reading a board needs the \`read\` scope; creating a card needs \`queue\` — a token minted
without them is refused here rather than at claim time. What an agent may queue, and onto
which boards, is also set per agent: \`supi agent queueing <agentId>\`.
",
  "stdout": "",
}
`;

