exports[`supi help, pinned > supi (no arguments) 1`] = `
{
  "exit": 0,
  "requests": [],
  "stderr": "",
  "stdout": "supi — SuperPipeline from a terminal (\`superpipeline\` is the same command)

Signing in and the binary:
  supi login                         sign in to this server's organization plane (device flow)
  supi logout                        forget that sign-in on this machine
  supi whoami                        who the stored token says you are
  supi help [<verb> [<sub-verb>]]    this summary, or one command in full (also supi <verb> --help)
  supi version                       print this binary's version
  supi skill [install [--dir <dir>]] print the agent skill, or install it into a skills directory
  supi update [--check]              replace this binary with the newest release

Boards and pipelines:
  supi boards                        the workspace's boards
  supi board <boardId>               one board: its stages and their cards
  supi templates                     the starting pipelines --template accepts
  supi create-board <name> [--template <id>] [--stages <file|->]
                                     create a board; --template defaults to simple
  supi set-stages <boardId> <file|-> replace a board's pipeline
  supi set-stale <boardId> [--hours <n>] [--off] [--on]
                                     set when a board's waiting cards count as stale, or switch it off
  supi set-stage <boardId> <stageKey> [--instructions <file|->] [--clear-instructions]
        [--name <name>] [--gate none|approval] [--wip <n>|none] [--owner <capability>]
        [--completion <file|->] [--clear-completion] [--return-stage <stageKey>]
        [--clear-return-stage]
                                     change ONE stage, leaving the others alone

Cards:
  supi card <boardId> <cardId>       one card in full
  supi create-card <boardId> <title> [--spec <file|->] [--priority <n>] [--due YYYY-MM-DD]
        [--label <id>...]
                                     queue a card, with this token as its grant
  supi edit-card <boardId> <cardId> [--title <text>] [--spec <file|->] [--merge-spec <file|->]
        [--priority <n>] [--due YYYY-MM-DD|none]
                                     change a card's title, spec, priority or due date
  supi move <boardId> <cardId> <stageKey>
                                     move a card to another stage
  supi resume <boardId> <cardId> --comment <text> [--stage <key>]
                                     send a card that is waiting on a person back to work, with a comment
  supi stale [--hours <n>]           cards stuck waiting, across every board in the workspace
  supi archive <boardId> <cardId>    archive a card, so the "show archived" filter has something to show
  supi log <boardId> <cardId>        what an agent did on a card, and its handoff

Comments on a card:
  supi comment <boardId> <cardId> <text>
                                     add a comment to a card
  supi comments <boardId> <cardId>   read a card's comments

Approval gates:
  supi gates <boardId>               approval gates waiting on a human
  supi approve <boardId> <gateId> [--comment "why"] [--delivery manual|automatic]
                                     approve a gate, choosing delivery for a frozen post
  supi delivery <boardId> <gateId> [--mode manual|automatic] [--live-url https://…]
        [--remind-at ISO timestamp]
                                     update delivery of an approved frozen post
  supi reject <boardId> <gateId> [--comment "why"]
                                     reject a gate
  supi request-changes <boardId> <gateId> --comment "what to change"
                                     send the card back for rework, saying what to change

Links between cards:
  supi link add <boardId> <fromCardId> <toCardId> --kind blocks|relates|parent|supersedes
        [--to-board <boardId>]
                                     declare an edge between two cards
  supi link rm <boardId> <fromCardId> <toCardId> --kind blocks|relates|parent|supersedes
        [--to-board <boardId>]
                                     remove an edge
  supi link list <boardId> <cardId>  every edge touching a card — same-board and cross-board, kept apart

Labels:
  supi label list                    the workspace's label catalogue
  supi label add <name> <colour>     declare a label
  supi label rm <id>                 remove a label (cards keep the stale id)

Projects and milestones:
  supi project list                  the workspace's projects (group cards across boards)
  supi project add <name> [--description <text>] [--target YYYY-MM-DD] [--lead <userId>]
                                     declare a project
  supi project show <projectId>      a project with its milestones, in order
  supi project rm <projectId>        remove a project (cards keep the stale id)
  supi milestone add <projectId> <name> [--target YYYY-MM-DD] [--sort <n>]
                                     add a milestone to a project
  supi milestone rm <milestoneId>    remove a milestone (cards keep the stale id)

Recurring cards:
  supi schedule list <boardId>       the board's recurring cards
  supi schedule add <boardId> --title <t> --rule <r> --tz <tz> [--stage <key>] [--priority <n>]
        [--overlap skip|allow]
                                     declare a schedule
  supi schedule rm <boardId> <scheduleId>
                                     remove a schedule
  supi schedule pause <boardId> <scheduleId>
                                     stop a schedule firing, keeping it
  supi schedule resume <boardId> <scheduleId>
                                     start a paused schedule firing again

Workspace, agents and capabilities:
  supi forge [<host>|none]           this workspace's forge host, shown or set
  supi agents                        the workspace's agents and what they declare
  supi agent create --name <name> --capability <key>... --external-id prn_… [--concurrency <n>]
                                     create an agent, linked to its principal as it is made
  supi agent mint-token <agentId> --kind claim-run|run-only [--out FILE]
                                     mint an agent's token: claim-run or run-only, shown once
  supi agent queueing <agentId> [--owner <userId>|none] [--boards <id,id,…>|none]
        [--ceiling <n>]
                                     what an agent may queue of its OWN: owner, boards, cards an hour
  supi capabilities                  the capability registry, with each one's origin
  supi capability define <id|key> --definition <text>
                                     say what a capability means, declaring it if it is new
  supi implications                  what one capability implies about another

  --json                             machine-stable output, on any command
  supi help <verb> [<sub-verb>]      one command in full (or: supi <verb> --help)

Credential, first found wins: $SUPERPIPELINE_AGENT_TOKEN_FILE, $SUPERPIPELINE_AGENT_TOKEN,
$SUPERPIPELINE_TOKEN, $AGENTPOD_TOKEN, \`supi login\`'s cached token, \`supi login\`'s device
credential (exchanged at the sign-in service), then \`fleet login\`'s token and device.
An agent acts with $SUPERPIPELINE_AGENT_TOKEN_FILE (a file, re-read every run) or
$SUPERPIPELINE_AGENT_TOKEN, either outranking every person's credential. An spa_ token reads
and plans; only an agent JWT (a station token) carries the dispatch grant that queues work and
moves cards, and it lives minutes — so point the FILE at something that keeps it fresh.

What you may do is your role in the workspace, which the server decides — not this command.
A refusal comes back as a 403 and is printed as it arrives. Exit status: 0 on success, 1 otherwise.
Reference: https://docs.superpipeline.dev/reference/cli/
",
}
`;

