  an agent token: any, no scope needed

Calls:
  GET /v1/boards/:boardId/gates/pending

Examples:
  supi gates brd_8f2c…
",
}
`;

exports[`supi help, pinned > supi help help 1`] = `
{
  "exit": 0,
  "requests": [],
  "stderr": "",
  "stdout": "supi help [<verb> [<sub-verb>] ]

With no argument, the summary of every command. With a verb, that command's synopsis, flags,
access and examples — the same text the reference pages are generated from. supi <verb> --help
and supi <verb> <sub-verb> --help print the same thing without running the command. -h and
--help alone are the summary.

Arguments:
  <verb>                a command, with its sub-verb if it has one (help link add)

Who may run it:
  Local: sends no credential to SuperPipeline.

Examples:
  supi help
  supi help schedule add
  supi set-stage --help
",
}
`;

